# ArtifactFlow fleet topology — Phase D (决策 7:单机/多机同一连续谱).
#
# For the common single-host case, prefer:
#   deploy/scripts/fleet.sh init-local
# It writes deploy/fleet.conf with the local arch and seeds deploy/.env from the
# intranet template. Copy/edit this file manually for custom or multi-host
# layouts. fleet.sh reads it to know which role runs on which host.
#
# To enable sandbox tools from a bundle that includes --with-sandbox:
#   sudo env AF_SANDBOX_POOL_SIZE=80G deploy/scripts/fleet.sh prepare-sandbox .
#   AF_ENABLE_SANDBOX=1 deploy/scripts/fleet.sh deploy .
#
# ── Format ──
# One row per (role, host). Blank lines and `#` comments ignored.
# Columns:  <role>  <host>  [arch=arm64|amd64]  [scale=N]
#   role   one of: infra | release | app | lb   (see below)
#   host   an ssh-reachable hostname/IP, OR the literal `local`
#          (= run right here, no ssh — the single-box degenerate case)
#   arch   target CPU arch; fleet.sh VALIDATES it against the bundle's
#          manifest Platform + the host's `uname -m` (loud-fail on mismatch).
#          release.sh emits one arch per build. Homogeneous fleet is the
#          assumption; build either x86 or arm with release.sh --platform.
#   scale  app rows only: number of backend replicas (frontend stays 1 —
#          only backend is the multi-replica, Redis-coordinated tier).
#
# ── Roles ──
#   infra    postgres + redis  (compose --profile infra; omit row for
#            external/managed DB — then set DATABASE_URL/REDIS_URL in .env)
#   release  the ONE host that runs the one-shot migrate+reconcile (release
#            service) under the PG advisory lock. Exactly one release row.
#   app      backend (×scale) + frontend. One row per app host.
#   lb       caddy reverse proxy / LB entry. Exactly one lb row.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Single machine — the common case. Every role on `local`, no ssh at all.
# This is the degenerate form of the multi-host sequence: fleet.sh runs the
# SAME deploy序列, transport just resolves to local execution.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
infra    local
release  local
app      local   arch=arm64  scale=2
lb       local

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Two machines — comment out the single-box block above and uncomment this.
# Control host runs fleet.sh and ssh's to k1/k2 (see deploy/FLEET.md).
# NOTE: cross-host is authored but UNEXERCISED until a 2nd machine exists —
# read the "Multi-host: unexercised seams" section of FLEET.md before relying
# on it (backend port publishing, static Caddy upstream, per-host DB URLs).
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# infra    k1   arch=arm64
# release  k1
# app      k1   arch=arm64  scale=2
# app      k2   arch=arm64  scale=2
# lb       k1   arch=arm64
